  "base_commit": "8721faaf9e7a6464df32a74a6fa0e9ff6435e878",
  "pr_number": 173,
  "issue_number": 172,
  "issue_title": "registry_gate: a malformed datasets/registry.jsonl line crashes the gate instead of rejecting it",
  "issue_body": "### What happens\n\n`eval.registry_gate.gate_registry_submission` collects schema issues from `validate_registry_entry` **without early-returning**, then unconditionally calls `check_registry_duplicates`, which does:\n\n```python\nrepo = hf_repo_from_url(entry[\"hf_url\"])\nsha = entry[\"trajectories_sha256\"]\n```\n\nwith no guard. A registry line that is missing `hf_url` / `trajectories_sha256`, or has a malformed `hf_url`, therefore raises `KeyError` / `ValueError` **before** the collected validation issues can be returned. `gate_registry_submission` also parses `entry[\"hf_url\"]` for the report's `hf_repo` field with the same exposure.\n\nNet effect: a typo'd or incomplete `datasets/registry.jsonl` line makes the `dataset_registry.yml` CI gate fail with a Python traceback, instead of the intended clean `dataset:REJECT` label + auto-close comment naming the exact problem.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```\n[missing hf_url]  check_registry_duplicates CRASHED: KeyError: 'hf_url'\n[malformed hf_url] check_registry_duplicates CRASHED: ValueError: hf_url must be https://huggingface.co/datasets/<org>/<repo>, got 'not-a-url'\ngate_registry_submission CRASHED: KeyError: 'hf_url'\n```\n\nThis is the same class of case `test_gate_registry_pr_rejects_schema_before_hf` already guards for `rows_total=0` \u2014 a schema-invalid entry should be reported, not crash.\n\n### Expected\n\nMalformed/missing `hf_url` or `trajectories_sha256` should yield a clean `dataset:REJECT` with the validation issue (which `validate_registry_entry` already produces), not an uncaught exception.\n\n### Fix\n\nPR follows: guard the duplicate check and the `hf_repo` lookup against fields `validate_registry_entry` already flags. Adds regression tests for missing and malformed `hf_url`.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-19T13:19:14.000Z",
